# Keep shell scripts and the machine-read data files LF in the working tree on
# every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF: the
# blank line in a .tsv becomes a lone carriage return, which reads as a record
# with an empty first field rather than as a blank line, and the checkers
# reject their own inventories. Linux CI never reproduces it, so the failure
# only ever appears on a contributor's machine.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
